            "subject": "LU-20099 nrs: dispatch BRW requests in per-object batches"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-11 21:24:57.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-11 21:50:01.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "subject": "LU-20099 nrs: cache pages that queued reads will read again",
        "message": "LU-20099 nrs: cache pages that queued reads will read again\n\nWhen the clients of a job read one file at the same time, such as an\ninput file, osd-ldiskfs reads each page from storage for every client\nonce the file is larger than readcache_max_filesize, or the read is\nreadcache_max_io_mb or larger, because it reads into pages of its own\nthat it does not cache.\n\nThe batches of the TBF and mClock policies queue the reads of an\nobject in offset order, so the class bucket can tell when another\nqueued read of the object shares a page with the read it dispatches.\nnrs_class_req_pop() then sets nr_read_shared on the request.  It looks\nat the queued requests next to the offset of the read, in its round\nand in the next round, which are the only rounds queued, so the check\nstays cheap.  ofd_preprw_read() passes the new DT_BUFS_TYPE_SHARED to\ndt_bufs_get() for such a read, and osd-ldiskfs caches its pages\nwhatever the size of the read and of the file, unless the read cache\nis off.  The queued reads then find the pages in the cache.\n\nOnly the reads of one class bucket are compared, so reads of clients\nin other classes or CPU partitions, and reads that are not queued\nyet, still read the pages again.  DoM reads on an MDT are not changed.\n\nAdd sanityn test_77tm, which reads a file larger than\nreadcache_max_filesize with one O_DIRECT reader and then with eight.\nThe readers share a group lock, as the client otherwise serializes\nO_DIRECT reads of one page.  One reader reads all 1024 pages from\nstorage.  Eight readers find 7104-7168 of their 8192 pages in the\ncache, and none without this patch.\n\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanityn env=ONLY=77\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm,llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Id90693c3670646a79eb83b152fd9e821e7500c1e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
